        <owl:annotatedTarget>CD8-positive, alpha-beta thymocytes are a subset of newly developed T cells found within the thymus. This cell type is characterized by the expression of the surface proteins CD8 and T-cell receptor alpha-beta (TCR αβ). T-cell receptors are integral to the function of the T cell, allowing it to recognize and bind to specific antigens presented by other cells, while expression of the CD8 TCR coreceptor designates them as precursors to cytotoxic T cells.
