        <owl:annotatedTarget>Mature NK T cells, or natural killer T cells, are a unique subset of alpha-beta T cells that serve as mediators in the immune response. They are named for their distinct ability to express markers typical of natural killer (NK) cells (such as NK1.1) as well as a T cell receptor specific for a limited set of ligands.
