        <owl:annotatedTarget>Mammary gland epithelial cells, also known as mammary epithelial cells, are essential cell types in the tissue of mammary glands, which are milk-producing glands in female mammals. They can be categorized into two types: luminal epithelial cells and myoepithelial cells, each with their distinct functions in milk processing and delivery.
