        <owl:annotatedTarget>Kidney capillary endothelial cells form the innermost lining of the capillaries and microvessels within kidneys, including those lining the glomerular capillaries and the vasa recta. Each cell exhibits a unique array of adhesion molecules, receptors, and secreted mediators which interact with circulating blood cells and solutes. 
